From a7b170eba2cebe5eaa42231e6c77839d30778600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 09:07:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pick the image provider on evidence, and say what it cost

Image generation had one static default and a fallback list ordered only by
circuit-breaker state. It now scores every configured provider per request on
recent success rate, observed latency, relative price and an editorial quality
tier, and logs why the winner won. Health stays a hard partition rather than a
weight, so an open breaker can never outrank a working provider no matter how
the weights are tuned later. Admins get "Auto" in the provider picker plus the
live ranking, visible before they commit to it.

The metering side was worse than under-detailed: streamed text asked for no
usage block at all, so every streamed caption and campaign was recorded with
NULL tokens and NULL cost. Streaming now asks for usage, and usage_events
carries time-to-first-token, the cached-prompt and reasoning-token subsets, and
which link in the fallback chain served the request with a sentence explaining
why.

ASR fallbacks are ranked by the same scorer instead of merely partitioned.

